From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos990: USI16 SPI boot channel for the Shannon S5123 modem

Add the PERIC1 USI16 block in SPI mode (sysreg_peric1 + 0x1048) with the
exynos850-spi controller at 0x10960000 (IRQ 434, LineageOS spi_16) and a
spidev child on CS0 at 2.15 MHz (LineageOS cpboot_spi@0), using the
existing spi16_bus/spi16_cs_func pin groups.

USI SPI has no prescaler and divides ipclk by 4. CMU_PERIC1 is not
modelled, so the clock is a fixed 8.67 MHz that userspace must provide by
selecting OSC 26 MHz (0x10700690 bit 4 = 0) and DIVRATIO 2 (0x10701820).

Tested on r8s kernel #13: sending the radio BOOT section (64400 B) over
/dev/spidev0.0 after the power_on_cp() GPIO sequence makes the CP drive
ps_hold and cp2ap_wakeup high within ~200 ms; without it both stay low.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos990.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos990.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos990.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos990.dtsi
@@ -436,6 +436,14 @@
 	/* Touch (S6SY761) helpers: the PERIC1 sub-CMU isn't modelled, so stub
 	 * the HSI2C clock; the two rails are real S2MPS19 LDOs (enabled via ACPM),
 	 * the fixed-regulators just satisfy the driver's vdd/avdd bulk-get. */
+	/* USI16 ipclk once userspace selects OSC 26 MHz / 3 (see usi_cpboot). */
+	usi16_spi_clk: usi16-spi-clock {
+		compatible = "fixed-clock";
+		#clock-cells = <0>;
+		clock-frequency = <8666666>;
+		clock-output-names = "usi16_spi_clk";
+	};
+
 	tsp_i2c_clk: tsp-i2c-clock {
 		compatible = "fixed-clock";
 		#clock-cells = <0>;
@@ -733,6 +741,47 @@
 				};
 			};
 		};
+
+		/* USI16 SPI: boot channel to the Shannon S5123 modem (LineageOS spi_16 +
+		 * cpboot_spi@0, 2.15 MHz, mode 0, 8 bit). The USI SPI has no internal
+		 * prescaler (clk_from_cmu) and divides ipclk by 4; CMU_PERIC1 is not
+		 * modelled, so userspace sets USI16 mux = OSC 26 MHz and DIVRATIO = 2
+		 * (0x10700690 / 0x10701820) to make ipclk 8.67 MHz -> SCLK 2.17 MHz.
+		 * shortcut: fixed-clock + manual CMU writes, upgrade to a CMU_PERIC1 driver. */
+		usi_cpboot: usi@109600c0 {
+			compatible = "samsung,exynos850-usi";
+			reg = <0x109600c0 0x20>;
+			ranges;
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <1>;
+			clocks = <&usi16_spi_clk>, <&usi16_spi_clk>;
+			clock-names = "pclk", "ipclk";
+			samsung,sysreg = <&sysreg_peric1 0x1048>;
+			samsung,mode = <2>; /* USI_V2_SPI */
+			status = "okay";
+
+			spi_16: spi@10960000 {
+				compatible = "samsung,exynos850-spi";
+				reg = <0x10960000 0x30>;
+				interrupts = <GIC_SPI 434 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+				clocks = <&usi16_spi_clk>, <&usi16_spi_clk>;
+				clock-names = "spi", "spi_busclk0";
+				pinctrl-names = "default";
+				pinctrl-0 = <&spi16_bus &spi16_cs_func>;
+				num-cs = <1>;
+				samsung,spi-src-clk = <0>;
+				#address-cells = <1>;
+				#size-cells = <0>;
+				status = "okay";
+
+				/* Raw access for the CP boot loader; spidev needs a listed compatible. */
+				cpboot@0 {
+					compatible = "rohm,dh2228fv";
+					reg = <0>;
+					spi-max-frequency = <2150000>;
+				};
+			};
+		};
 
 		/* PERIC0 system registers — the exynos-usi driver writes USI mode (I2C)
 		 * here to mux the display sub-PMIC bus. */
